  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off scheduled for June 15th. The initial budget was $500,000, but it was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration. The project team was expanded in September with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. In July, the team gathered ideas to leverage AI for data visualization, with proposals due by July 20th. A significant milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, which occurred ahead of schedule. The next phase involves user interface enhancements starting in October. Additionally, specific budgets have been approved for compliance ($55,000) and training ($15,000). A celebration for the milestone is planned for October 10th."
